   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to exempting\nthe Southwood Volunteer Fire Department, Inc. from the requirement that the\npercentage of non-resident fire department members not exceed forty-five\npercent of the membership",
    "basePrintNo": "S4714",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4714-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1402, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4714\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to\nexempting the Southwood Volunteer Fire Department, Inc. from the\nrequirement that the percentage of non-resident fire department members\nnot exceed forty-five percent of the membership\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize non-resident volunteer membership within the Southwood\nVolunteer Fire Department, Inc.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subparagraph 3 of paragraph (c) of section 1402 of the\nnot-for-profit corporation law.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Southwood Volunteer Fire Department, Inc. has had difficulty\nrecruiting members from their district and is close to exceeding the\nforty-five percent cap.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
